      'New “Diddle while waiting” choice (RTTY, on by default): the RX/TX button at the bottom (or Pause) puts the station on the air even with an empty box and keeps it there until you press it again; while it waits for text Aurora sends the diddle like MMTTY and fldigi, and with the choice off it sends only the idle tone. You change it in the mode settings, in the “RTTY settings” window and in the mode menu. New CW output “TCI (radio CWX)”: the text of the macros goes to the radio’s CWX with the TCI command “cw_macros” (Flex, ExpertSDR), which does CW, PTT and key by itself; not tested with a real radio. “Support Aurora” now has a small note saying the donation is free and voluntary, with nothing given in return. New Linux packages also for 64-bit ARM (Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, the Pi 5 with 4 GB or more is recommended; not yet tested on a real Raspberry Pi): guide in the repository (docs/raspberry.md).',
